<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Damavand</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Damavand is a town and district in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alborz">Alborz</a> mountains of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a>, at the foot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-damavand">Mount Damavand</a>. In the early Islamic period it was ruled by the Masmughans, local lords of Iranian descent, until the Abbasid conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabaristan">Tabaristan</a> in 759–760. It lay on the route between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a> and the Caspian lowlands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damavand.jpg" alt="Damavand" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Safa.daneshvar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:981012-Damavand-South-IMG_9861-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
